      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.15,
          "end": 2.07,
          "en": "-: In this video we'll talk about Stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.22,
          "en": "Now, Stack is basically a Linear Data Structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.22,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "so we can use it to store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "Now the question arise, \"Why it is different.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 11.94,
          "en": "The thing is Stack follows something called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.94,
          "end": 14.13,
          "en": "Last IN, First OUT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.13,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "So as you have seen, basically we were able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "to Stack data on top of other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "So here we were using devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "but we can also store data in the same format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "So basically, what happens is you can create a Stack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "but then Stack looks something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "Basically, you have this type of memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "where you only have one entry point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "and the same entry point is also an exit point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "So let's say if you have some list of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 39.12,
          "en": "which you want to store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 39.12,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "So maybe I want to store five, eight, six, three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 44.97,
          "en": "So I want to store these four values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 47.94,
          "en": "Now what happens is when you want to store this five,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "this five basically goes into the Stack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "but the question is where it will be stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.2,
          "en": "So it will be stored somewhere here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "So five will be here, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "And now once you store the five,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "now you want to store a eight.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "It goes on top of five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "So eight goes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "Now what happens here is it follows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "as I mentioned, it follows LIFO,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 69.69,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "which is Last IN, First OUT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 74.82,
          "en": "Basically, the last element which have entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 74.82,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "will be the first element which will come out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 78.27,
          "en": "just like stack of books",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 78.27,
          "end": 80.43,
          "en": "or stack of devices or stack of plates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "So the last thing which went inside, which is eight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 86.64,
          "en": "is the first thing to come out, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 86.64,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "So we use a concept called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "Push and Pop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "So when you want to insert data, we use Push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "When you want to get data out, we use Pop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 99.69,
          "en": "So at this point, if I say, \"Hey, this is my Stack,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 101.31,
          "en": "let's say Stack is NUMs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 101.31,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "And if I say, \"Hey, NUMs, Pop.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "So what NUMs will do is it will give you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "the last element entered, which is eight, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "But let's say you enter some more data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "you want to insert six as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 114.03,
          "en": "So six goes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 114.03,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "Now, when six goes there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 116.707,
          "en": "basically, when you say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 116.707,
          "end": 120.15,
          "en": "\"Hey, I want to Pop now,\" so you have, it'll give you six.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "So if you want to insert data, you will say Push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 125.76,
          "en": "When you want to get data out, we use Pop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 129.03,
          "en": "Basically, we have certain terms you have to remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "What if the Stack is full?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 133.59,
          "en": "So let's say the size of this Stack is four",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 133.59,
          "end": 134.423,
          "en": "or maybe three instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 134.423,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "Let's say the Stack, the size of this stack is three,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "and now you have entered three values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "But what if you are entering a new value?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "So instead of three, let's have some other values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 143.64,
          "en": "so that you will not get confused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 146.19,
          "en": "with the size of the Stack and the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 146.19,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "Let's say the value is nine here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "So when you are inserting nine now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "now we don't have a space, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "So nine, when you try to Push nine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "it will give you an error called, Overflow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "and you might have seen this error, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "Which is called Stack Overflow, the website?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 164.31,
          "en": "It came from this word, which is Overflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 166.11,
          "en": "So the Stack overflowing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 166.11,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "So nine is not able to save there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 171.03,
          "en": "Also, there's one more term called, Underflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 171.863,
          "en": "Now what is Underflow?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 171.863,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "Let's say you have a stack which is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 174.45,
          "en": "So we are getting a new stack here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "which is empty in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 178.41,
          "en": "And when you say, \"Hey, I have an empty stack here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 178.41,
          "end": 179.31,
          "en": "I want to Pop.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 179.31,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "Now we can only Pop the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "when they are there, it's not there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "So we don't have an element there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "So it will give you another, which is Underflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "So Overflow when you have a Stack full,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 192.54,
          "en": "but still you're trying to insert data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "And Underflow is basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 196.35,
          "en": "where you don't have any elements there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 196.35,
          "end": 198.9,
          "en": "but you still try to fetch data or remove data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 198.9,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "So one thing to remember with Pop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.19,
          "en": "Pop is basically, a function or a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 203.19,
          "end": 205.07999999999998,
          "en": "to get the element out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 205.07999999999998,
          "end": 206.85,
          "en": "So of course, it will give you the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 206.85,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "That also means that the element is coming out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "So example, let's say at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.17000000000002,
          "en": "I want to do a Pop on this Stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 214.17000000000002,
          "end": 215.55,
          "en": "Basically, what I'm also doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 215.55,
          "end": 217.82999999999998,
          "en": "is I'm Popping this six out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 217.82999999999998,
          "end": 219.607,
          "en": "So now, if you say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 219.607,
          "end": 221.04,
          "en": "\"How many elements I have in this stack?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 222.66,
          "en": "Only two, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 225.24,
          "en": "And again, if you say Pop on this particular NUMs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "it will take this eight out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 228.96,
          "en": "at which came with the underscore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 228.96,
          "end": 230.52,
          "en": "but that's not how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "Let me just do that again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 234,
          "en": "So eight will come out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 234,
          "end": 236.91,
          "en": "Again, when you say Pop, the five will come out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 240.6,
          "en": "Again, when you say Pop, it will give you an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 243.78,
          "en": "which is the Underflow error or Underflow exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 243.78,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "So basically, Pop means getting the data out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 248.55,
          "en": "But let's say you don't want to get the data out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 248.55,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "you just want to see what is a last element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 254.76,
          "en": "So we use one more thing for that, which is called, Peek.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 254.76,
          "end": 257.25,
          "en": "Now, Peek will give you the last value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 257.25,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "but it will not remove the value from the Stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "So if you just want to check, you want to Peek,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 263.07,
          "en": "you can use Peek.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 263.07,
          "end": 266.31,
          "en": "But if you want to get the element out, use a Pop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 266.31,
          "end": 268.26,
          "en": "When you want to insert data, you say Push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 268.26,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "So this is your Last IN, First OUT inside Stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 272.063,
          "en": "Now, question arise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 272.063,
          "end": 273.72,
          "en": "\"How we are going to implement this?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "So there are two ways of implementing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 278.22,
          "en": "One, you can use Normal Array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 278.22,
          "end": 280.42,
          "en": "In fact, in Array itself, we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 281.64,
          "end": 285.69,
          "en": "Fixed Size Array or we can use Dynamic Array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 285.69,
          "end": 287.64,
          "en": "Now in Fixed Size, basically, by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 287.64,
          "end": 289.83,
          "en": "in most of the languages, when you say Array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 289.83,
          "end": 292.62,
          "en": "it's a Fixed Size, but you can make it Dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 292.62,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "So you can expand the Stack or the Array the way you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
